d":"baptize","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to perform the Christian sacrament of baptism","word":"batizar"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to dedicate or christen","word":"batizar"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"I vvas baptized in thy Cordiall vvater, againſt Original ſinne, and I haue drunke of thy Cordiall Blood, for my recouerie, from actuall, and habituall ſinne, in the other Sacrament.","ref":"1624, John Donne, “11. Prayer.”, in Deuotions upon Emergent Occasions, and Seuerall Steps in My Sicknes: […], London: […] A[ugustine] M[atthews] for Thomas Iones, →OCLC, pages 280–281:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[7,15]],"id":"db718f40-8521-48ef-827b-9c764746f773"}],"topics":["Christianity"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Christianity"],"links":[["Christianity","Christianity"],["sacrament","sacrament"],["baptism","baptism"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"christen"},{"word":"full"}],"raw_glosses":["(Christianity) To perform the sacrament of baptism by sprinkling or pouring water over someone or immersing them in water."],"glosses":["To perform the sacrament of baptism by sprinkling or pouring water over someone or immersing them in water."],"tags":["British","English","Oxford","US"],"id":"a25936d1-d0c8-40d9-b38f-a61b56967d48"},{"examples":[{"text":"Ample evidence for this transfer of divine imagery can be found in early Christian times, when the Mother of God took over the titles, shrines, iconography and power of the great mother goddess of the Mediterranean world. This \"baptizing\" of pagan imagery was a successful missionary strategy that allowed Christianity to attract peoples accustomed to female deities while still maintaining faith in God as Father, Son and Holy Spirit","ref":"2000 June 17, Elizabeth A. Johnson, “Mary of Nazareth: Friend of God and Prophet”, in America, volume 182, number 21:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[228,237]],"id":"3f618795-0263-436d-baae-4cfe38560681"}],"links":[["Christianize","Christianize"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"raw_glosses":["(figurative) To Christianize."],"glosses":["To Christianize."],"tags":["British","English","Oxford","US","figuratively"],"id":"60dd102d-9167-4fbc-b7bb-be3578e7572c"},{"links":[["dedicate","dedicate"],["christen","christen"]],"glosses":["To dedicate or christen."],"tags":["British","English","Oxford","US"],"id":"1b9f2cdd-4ad5-4b2c-bdfe-b10fecf7106e"},{"examples":[{"text":"There's a good tavern nearby where they don't baptize liquor!","ref":"1965, The Road to Santiago: Pilgrims of St. James, page 194:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[46,53]],"id":"c409df04-1c24-449a-b050-0611c4ce2437"},{"text":"In 1833 Charles Kingsley wrote of the Royal Victora Hall in the Waterloo Road as 'a licensed pit of darkness'. The darkness remained unrelieved until, in 1880, Miss Emma Cons took over the lease and baptized the drinks that were served at the bar and the songs that were sung on the stage.","ref":"1973, Robert Speaight, Shakespeare on the Stage:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[199,207]],"id":"b8be4c7e-c627-4d72-8399-9d1f5693d06a"},{"text":"The general practice in the West Indies was to baptize, add color, and otherwise adulterate rum to make it appear better.","ref":"2007, Walter Scott Dunn, Choosing Sides on the Frontier in the American Revolution, →ISBN, page 91:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[47,54]],"id":"661e6bd2-3391-41ee-96c9-d1d78782a9e5"}],"categories":["English slang","English terms with archaic senses","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["dilute","dilute"]],"raw_glosses":["(archaic, slang) Of rum, brandy, or any other spirits, to dilute with water."],"glosses":["Of rum, brandy, or any other spirits, to dilute with water."],"tags":["British","English","Oxford","US","archaic","slang"],"id":"82d0b5c6-3172-4cc0-8995-01a34e7ff194"},{"categories":["English slang"],"links":[["joint","joint"]],"raw_glosses":["(slang) To ensure proper burning of a joint by moistening the exterior with saliva."],"glosses":["To ensure proper burning of a joint by moistening the exterior with saliva."],"tags":["British","English","Oxford","US","slang"],"id":"f29aeaa8-a110-4fa5-875b-e58f91578bca"},{"examples":[{"text":"Nigga actin tough on the net, Imma baptize him, .223 shells and he’s shot like I am Mad Ryan\nPut him in a coffin, hold him one year, he is no longer\nFucking on an opp nigger, bitch he sayin “go longer!”","ref":"2022 April 26, “Bad for Business”, OTM ft. Young Bull (lyrics), 1:21:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[35,42]],"id":"18cea98e-114a-41ed-a717-b3683a14b963"},{"text":"I'm on frontstreet over them sides\nCatch an opp lackin', leave him baptised\nBro up the Glock, don't freeze\nBig rambo, inject with ease (Wet that)","ref":"2023 September 28, “Block Boy”, #Sinsquad Stewie (lyrics), 1:58:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[67,75]],"id":"b52d36d3-751f-4258-85fd-bad4234ece3c"}],"categories":["English slang","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["extinguish","extinguish"],["life","life"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"wax"},{"word":"wet"},{"word":"juice up"},{"word":"annihilate","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"bag","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"baptize","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"bereave of life","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"blight","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"bring down","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"bump off","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"bury","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"cack","source":"Thesaurus:kill","tags":["US","slang"]},{"word":"compromised to a permanent end","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"croak","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"crush","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"dash","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"deactivate","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"dead","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"demolish","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{"word":"destroy","source":"Thesaurus:kill"},{